<!-- Aura-SOC - rule 100680 (level 13). Domain: ransomware,threat_hunting,linux,
     Naming convention and load-order trap: see rules/README.md -->
<group name="ransomware,threat_hunting,linux,">

  <!-- ==== Mass data destruction (T1485 / T1561) ====
       The built-in rule 553 ("File deleted", level 7) is tagged T1485 but
       reasons per file: it does not tell an isolated deletion from a full wipe.
       And since our FIM is filtered by `restrict`, it hardly ever fires anyway.

       Two angles kept, same doctrine as the rest of the pack: we do not look for
       volume (counting deletions means watching all of /home -> the very noise we
       refused), we look for unambiguous INTENT.

       Angle rejected: auditing the unlink/unlinkat syscalls. Technically precise,
       but every deleted temporary file produces an event - unmanageable volume,
       same reasoning as for clone()/fork() in 100626.

       R6 T1561 - irreversible destruction of a storage device. None of these
       commands has a routine production use: they show up at provisioning time
       (fresh machine, no Wazuh agent yet) or during a malicious wipe.

       REVISION 2026-07-26: missing wipe tools added.
       - `hdparm` with the security-erase option (and its enhanced variant): ATA
         firmware erase, irreversible, and it touches no /dev path in a
         positional argument the former regex could recognise.
       - `nvme format` / `nvme sanitize`: the NVMe equivalent.
       - `sgdisk` with the zap-all option: destruction of the GPT partition tables.
       - `cryptsetup luksErase` / `luksKillSlot`: destruction of the LUKS
         keyslots. This is the cheapest wipe available to an attacker - a few
         kilobytes written make the whole volume permanently unreadable.
       - `badblocks -w`: destructive write across the whole device.
       The first four need no recognisable /dev/... positional argument, hence a
       dedicated alternative per verb. -->

  <rule id="100680" level="13">
    <if_group>audit</if_group>
    <regex type="pcre2">a0="(?:[^"]*/)?(?:(?i:wipefs|blkdiscard)"|(?i:mkfs)(?:\.[a-z0-9]+)?"|(?i:shred|dd|badblocks)"(?: a\d+="[^"]*")*? a\d+="(?:of=)?/dev/(?:sd|nvme|vd|hd|mapper|disk)|(?i:hdparm)"(?: a\d+="[^"]*")*? a\d+="--security-erase(?:-enhanced)?"|(?i:nvme)"(?: a\d+="[^"]*")*? a\d+="(?:format|sanitize)"|(?i:sgdisk)"(?: a\d+="[^"]*")*? a\d+="(?:--zap-all|-Z)"|(?i:cryptsetup)"(?: a\d+="[^"]*")*? a\d+="(?:luksErase|erase|luksKillSlot)")</regex>
    <description>Data destruction: low-level wipe of a storage device ($(audit.command))</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1561.001</id>
      <id>T1485</id>
    </mitre>
  </rule>

</group>
